<title>USA: McDonnell Douglas gets $22 million contract.</title>
<headline>McDonnell Douglas gets $22 million contract.</headline>
<dateline>ST. LOUIS 1997-07-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>McDonnell Douglas Corp said Thursday it received a contract to develop technology for a new air-to-air missile.</p>
<p>McDonnell Douglas said under the five-year $22 million includes the design, development and demonstration of an advanced flight control system. The contract is part of the U.S. Air Force's Air Superiority Missile Technology program.</p>
<p>Hughes Missile Systems Co will be the principal subcontractor to McDonnell Douglas, and Thiokol Corp will be the subcontractor for integrating and testing the program, the company said.</p>
<p>((--Chicago newsdesk, 312-408-8787))</p>
